      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax. To clear the 32 Msps throughput constraint and the 0.5 us p99-batch bound (32 back-to-back results must fit in 0.5 us, i.e. ~16 ns each at the operating clock), the design needs a high Fmax, which favors a moderate N. Accuracy <= 2^-12 is the binding accuracy constraint: with Q1.(W-2) output the LSB is 2^-(W-2), so W=14 already gives a 12-bit LSB and W=16 gives 14-bit; N in 12..16 with small guards keeps max_abs_err near/below 2^-12 while keeping the per-stage adder/shift chain short for Fmax. This is the primary family for the min-area corner since it has the fewest registers of the 1-result/cycle options."
    },
